the word more than once?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $11$ different letters in the word DOCUMENTARY, so $n=11.$ We want to select $3$ of those letters to make-up a $3$-letter word, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different made-up words is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{11}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{11!}{(11-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11!}{8!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot \\cancel{8!}}{\\cancel{8!}} \\\\  & =11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =990.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122477/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "256d3a08-0ade-51e9-887b-67250d5fae21"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
